course: dictionary
lesson: 4971
title: Income
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Income is the money that comes in. A person, family or business gets income from work, from selling things, or from other places, and it is usually counted per week, month or year. Pocket money is a child's income.
explain: «Self-employed people work for themselves; their income can go up and down from month to month, so they save in good months for slow ones.» The word income is the money coming in. The sentence tells you it can change, so a good month may bring more income than a slow one.
explain: Income is not the same as savings. Income minus spending equals savings. If you get £10 pocket money and spend £7, you have £3 left to save.
fact: Income is money coming in. Spending is money going out.
fact: Income can come from work, from selling things, or from other places.
fact: «Income tax» is money taken from wages before the worker gets it.
fact: «Mopane worms» are big caterpillars eaten in southern Africa. They are dried and stored for months, and they are an important food and income for families.
fact: Income minus spending equals savings.
exercise: «Self-employed people work for themselves; their income can go up and down from month to month.» What is income in this sentence? | A bank building where money is kept | The money going out on things they buy | A kind of tax paid on toys | *The money a person or business gets in over time
exercise: Pocket money is a child's income. Sam gets £10 pocket money and spends £7. How much is left to save? | £7 | *£3 | £10 | £17
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Mopane worms are big caterpillars eaten in southern Africa; they are dried, stored for months and are an important food and income for families.» that means money coming in. | stored | caterpillars | southern | *income
test: «Leo thinks jails, police and income tax have always been there.» What is income tax? | A kind of savings account | A payment for council bins | *A tax taken from wages | A tax on children's toys
test: A family has a low income. What does low income mean? | *Little money coming in | Money given free by shops to customers | Very high prices for food | Money saved in a bank for many years
exam: Mia earns £30 a week from a paper round and £5 a week from selling old toys. What is her weekly income? | £25 | £5 | £30 | *£35
